// Tokenize a byte slice into tokens for diffing.
// Each token is a (start, end) pair into the original slice.
// Token rules:
//   - Runs of [A-Za-z0-9_] are a single token (a "word")
//   - Each other byte is its own token (non-word single byte)
//   Whitespace runs ARE tokenized as: each ws byte its own token? No,
//   let's verify with observations.
//
